    "summary": "Bertha>Playin' jam and fiery Friend Of The Devil drive this high‑energy show",
    "blurb": "The Spectrum concert delivers a high‑energy first set highlighted by a crisp Friend Of The Devil and solid Althea. The second set explodes with the classic Bertha > Playing In The Band > Ship Of Fools sequence that rolls into an extended post‑Ship jam, drums and space. Audience recordings are good enough to capture the band’s tight interplay throughout.",
    "review": "What unfolds at The Spectrum on April 5, 1982 is a tightly wound, audience‑captured performance that still feels fresh decades later. Jerry’s voice shines on Friend Of The Devil and Ship Of Fools while his guitar fires on eight cylinders, especially during the soaring Bertha > Playing In The Band > Ship Of Fools trek that morphs into an adventurous post‑Ship jam before drums and space. Phil provides his usual steady bass foundation, anchoring the improvisations, and Brent’s keyboard textures add both sparkle before The Wheel and drive the momentum in the extended jam. The rhythm duo of Mickey and Billy lock in with crisp hi‑hat work and powerful drumming, keeping the flow tight even as the band stretches out. Highlights also include a spirited Althea, gritty Deep Elem Blues, and an engaging rendition of The Wheel that rounds out a setlist full of classic Dead storytelling.",
